
DNS A Record Cleanup Script (PowerShell)

A simple PowerShell utility to clean up stale DNS A records based on host validation results exported to CSV.

This script reads a validation report, identifies hosts marked as unreachable (IsPingable=False), and automatically removes their corresponding A records from a specified Microsoft DNS Forward Lookup Zone.

⚠️ Important
Run this script only locally on the DNS Server
Do NOT execute remotely
Ensure you have proper administrative permissions before running
Validate your CSV data before performing deletions
Features
Imports host validation results from CSV
Filters unreachable hosts (IsPingable=False)
Supports root records ((same as parent folder) → @)
Removes matching DNS A records
Displays progress and deletion count
Requirements
Windows Server with DNS Server role installed
PowerShell with DNS Server module available
Administrator privileges
Configuration

Update the following values before execution:

$csvPath = "C:\Path\to\dns-validation-report.csv"
$zone = "your-zone.com"
CSV Example
HostName,IsPingable
server01,false
server02,true
(same as parent folder),false
Usage
Export or prepare the DNS validation CSV.
Set the correct CSV path.
Configure your DNS zone.
Run the script directly on the DNS server.
Example Output
Rows with IsPingable=False: 12
Removing A record: server01
Removing A record: @
Disclaimer

This script permanently deletes DNS records using Remove-DnsServerResourceRecord -Force.

Always test in a non-production environment first and keep DNS backups before execution.
